{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":286172,"ns":0,"title":"Absorption law","extract":"In algebra, the absorption law or absorption identity is an identity linking a pair of binary operations.\nTwo binary operations, ¤ and ⁂, are said to be connected by the absorption law if:\n\na ¤ (a ⁂ b) = a ⁂ (a ¤ b) = a.","description":"Law in algebra","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}